{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114511-fix-peach-everything-you-do-is-worthless-nightmare","id":1114511,"title":"[Fix PEACH] Everything you do is worthless Nightmare","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T04:07:03-07:00","id":1114511,"title":"[Fix PEACH] Everything you do is worthless Nightmare","content":"This Nightmare is really cool on paper, but when used, it's lackluster. Giving &quot;7 successes for Exceptional Success&quot; doesn't convey the idea that what you do is worthless, and it's the basic effect of the Nightmare. It only gives the idea that excellence will be more difficult, but you usually don't need an Exceptional to do something.<br /> <br /> Here's my fix.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast chooses a type of action. This can be a trait category (Mental, Physical, Social), a particular field (combat, infiltration, research, etc.), or any other reasonably<br /> broad category. <u>Within that category of action, the victim\u2019s roll is penalyzed by -2.</u><br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The results of all of the victim\u2019s actions in the chosen category are listless, barely adequate, and uninspired. When the number of successes on a roll matters (for example, in combat or in an extended action), any successful roll is treated as though it scored only a single success. A rolled exceptional success counts as two successes. The victim may reflexively spend 1 Willpower to negate this effect for a single action.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> As long as the Nightmare is active, the Beast may spend 1 Satiety to reduce the victim to a chance die on a single roll.<br /> <u><b>Exceptional Success:</b> In addition, the victim\u2019s threshold for exceptional success on the action to 7 successes.</u><br /> <br /> What do you think about this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T04:20:07-07:00","id":1114517,"title":"","content":"This seems like &quot;you are incompetent&quot;. It's the difference between &quot;you're not a good enough doctor to save her&quot; and &quot;why bother saving her, she's going to die in the end anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> Maybe normal: Extra bonuses for Vice, and make playing to the target's vice more effective in social manoeuvring.<br /> High Satiety: Remove the mechanical benefits for one Aspiration (including beats) for a scene.<br /> Satity Expenditure: The target must succede on a roll to act in line with an Aspiration or their Virtue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:15:50-07:00","id":1117201,"title":"","content":"Gotta disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> here: I've always felt the same about the normal effect, and think penalizing an action by 2 is far from &quot;why bother saving her, she's going to die in the end anyway&quot;. I much prefer your version of Everything you do is Worthless!, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar316_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"316\" data-vbnamecard=\"316\">Jesuncolo</a>.<br /> +2 is something you could easily end up with for having the right tools/equipment, which would be negated with this, highlighting incompetence. Basically &quot;I have an excellent forge, and still my products are as good as what my neighbour churns out with his outdated, inefficient and broken stuff. I suck as a blacksmith -.-&quot; or &quot;I have superior ingredients and tools, and my dishes taste about as good as instant-noodles. I am a failure as a chef -.-&quot;<br /> The High Satiety effect has not been changed if I see that correctly (can't check right now). And is still not a &quot;why bother&quot; case imo: you can still save her, it'll just be harder/take longer and there is a higher chance of screwing up the longer the task is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T14:49:17-07:00","id":1117940,"title":"","content":"They way my group absolutely spams Inspired with strong characters, this nightmare is on a list of &quot;largely useless&quot; Between a mage in marriage oath to a Sunnikuse Bloodline grafter, and a physical monster and a skilled academic - most of the nightmares fall pretty flat since we typically roll around 10 successes even with significant penalties (especially since Willpower is no object and we can make what were good at Rote thanks to Professional Training)<br /> <br /> In a power game, Beasts don't really hold a candle to the others for their cross-contamination meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:17:34-07:00","id":1117952,"title":"","content":"I don't think that is their point. They are more for a Beast vs. Prey.<br /> <br /> Because, remember, a cross-over troupe is an absolute rarity in that world, and also not the easiest thing to play (someone will be left in the dust unless the ST makes sure everyone gets something they are good at).<br /> <br /> But yeah, I wouldn't mind a power upgrade for Beasts in cases like those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T12:41:14-07:00","id":1119055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114511-fix-peach-everything-you-do-is-worthless-nightmare?p=1117940#post1117940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They way my group absolutely spams Inspired with strong characters, this nightmare is on a list of &quot;largely useless&quot; Between a mage in marriage oath to a Sunnikuse Bloodline grafter, and a physical monster and a skilled academic - most of the nightmares fall pretty flat since we typically roll around 10 successes even with significant penalties (especially since Willpower is no object and we can make what were good at Rote thanks to Professional Training)<br /> <br /> In a power game, Beasts don't really hold a candle to the others for their cross-contamination meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast are actually pretty powerful. Just...not their Nightmares (besides Behold My True Form!). Their Atavisms are flexible and powerful. They are great at hiding, and can be great damage dealers. Also, the possibility to create Tilts from their Lair. That said, Mages are simply up a couple notches in power and flexibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T16:26:35-07:00","id":1119358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114511-fix-peach-everything-you-do-is-worthless-nightmare?p=1119055#post1119055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast are actually pretty powerful. Just...not their Nightmares (besides Behold My True Form!). Their Atavisms are flexible and powerful. They are great at hiding, and can be great damage dealers. Also, the possibility to create Tilts from their Lair. That said, Mages are simply up a couple notches in power and flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I feel like that is the exact reason Nightmares are often overlooked: they have less potential for fights between supernaturals. I'd really like to see them being a tad stronger, so that playing a high-satiety Beast would be more intriguing. Fun way to do that could be to drop supernatural tolerance out of the equation, forcing a kind of &quot;nightmares work on everyone equally&quot; scenario, but that would be pretty overpowered, huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T20:54:11-07:00","id":1119393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114511-fix-peach-everything-you-do-is-worthless-nightmare?p=1119358#post1119358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I feel like that is the exact reason Nightmares are often overlooked: they have less potential for fights between supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not really <i>for</i> fights, is the thing; they're weighted toward the end of the Satiety scale where you're more strongly encouraged to work subtly and use proxies and just sort of generally play the indirect game while you occasionally make Chambers or claim new assets.<br /> <br /> Denying a specialist easy access to the Inspired Condition is pretty major, as is holding up accelerated progress on an extended action or just maintaining an open channel to immediately remove the target's entire dicepool at cost; being the catch-all category for every focused mental influence power a Beast can have means Nightmares are going to include abilities that occupy a more particular niche than dealing damage or compelling specific activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T07:50:04-07:00","id":1119506,"title":"","content":"Make it so that every success is poisoned, incuring a negative effect as though it were a dramatic failure. This does not negate the success, but often undermines it. Exceptional successes and failures don't trigger this penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T09:45:04-07:00","id":1119547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1114511-fix-peach-everything-you-do-is-worthless-nightmare?p=1119393#post1119393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not really <i>for</i> fights, is the thing; they're weighted toward the end of the Satiety scale where you're more strongly encouraged to work subtly and use proxies and just sort of generally play the indirect game while you occasionally make Chambers or claim new assets.<br /> <br /> Denying a specialist easy access to the Inspired Condition is pretty major, as is holding up accelerated progress on an extended action or just maintaining an open channel to immediately remove the target's entire dicepool at cost; being the catch-all category for every focused mental influence power a Beast can have means Nightmares are going to include abilities that occupy a more particular niche than dealing damage or compelling specific activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, you're right of course. As I said somewhere else, they are mostly something you can use to pursue your hunger, and most importantly, the nightmare is not the end-all-be-all: depending on your hunger, you cannot just go up to someone and use it on them (I mean, you probably could, but where is the fun in that?!). Instead, using it like a jab to soften up the target, and finish with others skills is a more effective (and satisfying imo) way to use them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1157\" data-vbnamecard=\"1157\">SoulGambit</a> You know, that's actually pretty interesting. Huh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}